HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Beverly is a 24-year-old female who presents for her yearly exam. The patient reports that she has been doing well. She started working in a bakery this summer which has been super fun. She has really been enjoying working there, but she finds herself, since she is so close to so many delicious treats, snacking a lot during shifts and eating a lot more desserts than she normally would. She has been taking her diabetes medication as prescribed. She has not missed any doses. She states that her diet has been pretty bad lately. She denies any weight loss or gain. She reports that her blood pressures have been good. She has been sleeping well, getting a full eight hours. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideation.

